# The Dockerfile ends in `COPY . .`, so anything not excluded here is baked
# into a published image layer — permanent and world-readable on a public
# registry, recoverable with `docker save` even if a later layer deletes it.

# --- Environment ----------------------------------------------------------
# `.env.local` carries NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL and NEXT_PUBLIC_MOCK_ROLE. The mock
# role is the one that matters: it seeds a fake authenticated user so pages
# render without a backend, and shipping it in an image would hand every
# visitor a pre-authenticated admin session in the UI.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- Dependencies and build output ----------------------------------------
# node_modules is reinstalled from package-lock.json in the image; copying the
# host's copy risks platform-specific binaries built for Windows.
node_modules/
.next/
out/
build/

# --- Residue --------------------------------------------------------------
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.eslintcache
coverage/

# --- Editor / OS ----------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
